DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Function ddwwaarrff__aadddd__ffddee__iinnsstt() adds a call frame instruction to the DWARF
     frame descriptor referenced by argument _f_d_e.

     Argument _f_d_e should reference a frame descriptor allocated using
     dwarf_new_fde(3).

     Argument _o_p specifies the operator for the frame instruction.  The DWARF
     standard defines the set of legal values for this argument.

     Argument _v_a_l_1 specifies the first operand of the frame instruction.

     Argument _v_a_l_2 specifies the second operand of the frame instruction.

     If argument _e_r_r is not NULL, it will be used to store error information
     in case of an error.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     On success, function ddwwaarrff__aadddd__ffddee__iinnsstt() returns the frame descriptor
     given in argument _f_d_e.  In case of an error, function
     ddwwaarrff__aadddd__ffddee__iinnsstt() returns DW_DLV_BADADDR and sets the argument _e_r_r.

EERRRROORRSS
     Function ddwwaarrff__aadddd__ffddee__iinnsstt() can fail with:

     [DW_DLE_ARGUMENT]                Argument _f_d_e was NULL.

     [DW_DLE_FRAME_INSTR_EXEC_ERROR]  The frame instruction operator specified
                                      in argument _o_p was invalid.

     [DW_DLE_MEMORY]                  An out of memory condition was encoun‐
                                      tered during the execution of the func‐
                                      tion.

